ground_truth.fix_description:
Do not permit checkpointer to be disabled (bit 6 unset) if chained signature is used. Revert in this case with custom error. Example fix in BaseSig.sol:
if (signatureFlag & 0x40 == 0) {
    revert MissingCheckpointer();
}

vulnerabilities.suggested_fix:
Enforce that chained signatures cannot bypass checkpointer validation. For example, in recover() before calling recoverChained():
- If (signatureFlag & 0x01 == 0x01) and the wallet is expected to be checkpointer-protected, require bit6 to be set and/or require a nonzero `_checkpointer`, otherwise revert with a custom error (e.g., `MissingCheckpointer()`).
Concretely (minimal):
```solidity
if ((signatureFlag & 0x01) == 0x01) {
  if ((signatureFlag & 0x40) == 0) revert MissingCheckpointer();
}
```
Additionally, ensure chained flow cannot skip snapshot retrieval when checkpointer is present (avoid always passing `_ignoreCheckpointer=true` for all segments unless snapshot was already validated and propagated safely).
